      "writtenOn": "2026-07-02T15:15:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The GXP is a custom SoC by HPE, and apparently they route the CPU to the BMC SoC directly. My suspicion is that they have some sort of SPI driver or mux internally which can\u0027t be controlled by the user.\n\nTheoretically, they also have something called `vrom`, which is a memory-mapped MTD that holds the BIOS and acts as a SPI for the host (i.e. the host boots from there.)\nHowever, we do not populate the `vrom` and it still works (still under discussion with HPE how this works within the SoC.)\n\nSo yes, this platform is cursed.",
      "parentUuid": "8a6ef119_4a17b58e",
      "revId": "7285b68bd6c1c78ab24d081a3a422921d9a2a86b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
